  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/5E75D8">Definition <span data-tag="5E75D8">5.5.3.2</span>.</a>presentable!fibrationfibration!presentable A map of simplicial sets $p: X \rightarrow S$ is a <em>presentable fibration</em> if it is both a Cartesian fibration and a coCartesian fibration, and each fiber $X_{s} = X \times _{S} \{ s\} $ is a presentable $\infty $-category. </p>
